{"family":"qb-x12-me-s1","course":"EXT1","year":12,"topic":"ME-S1","questions":[{"id":"X12-S1-002","group":"X12-S1-002","dp":"S1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":2,"title":"At least one","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(8,0.1)$. Find $P(X\\ge1)$ correct to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.5695,"tol":0.00005},"hints":["Use the complement.","P(X = 0) = 0.9⁸.","Subtract."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Use the complement.","method":"P(X = 0) = 0.9⁸.","worked":"Subtract."},"steps":[{"h":"Complement","d":"$1-0.9^{8}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.4305,"why":"That is P(X = 0)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"1 − P(X = 0)","line":"1-0.9^8"},{"marks":1,"point":"0.5695","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-005","group":"X12-S1-005","dp":"S1.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"How many trials","prompt":"Each trial succeeds with probability $0.2$, independently. Find the least number of trials for the probability of at least one success to exceed $0.95$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":14},"answerPrefix":"n =","hints":["Complement.","Logs flip the inequality.","Round up."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Complement.","method":"Logs flip the inequality.","worked":"Round up."},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$1-0.8^{n}>0.95\\Rightarrow n>\\tfrac{\\ln0.05}{\\ln0.8}\\approx13.4$"}],"traps":[{"value":13,"why":"Rounded down."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.8ⁿ < 0.05","line":"0.8^n < 0.05"},{"marks":1,"point":"14","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-015","group":"X12-S1-015","dp":"S1.1a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Winning a best of five","prompt":"A team wins each game independently with probability $0.6$. A series ends when one team has won $3$ games. Find the probability that the team wins the series.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.68256},"hints":["Series length 3, 4 or 5.","The deciding game is a win.","Choose where losses go."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Series length 3, 4 or 5.","method":"The deciding game is a win.","worked":"Win in 3, 4 or 5 games: last game a win"},"steps":[{"h":"Cases","d":"Win in 3, 4 or 5 games: last game a win"},{"h":"Sum","d":"$0.6^{3}\\left[1+\\binom31(0.4)+\\binom42(0.4)^{2}\\right]=0.68256$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.216,"why":"Only counted winning the first three games."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Last game must be a win","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Three cases","line":"0.6^3*(1+3*0.4+6*0.16)"},{"marks":1,"point":"0.68256","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-016","group":"X12-S1-016","dp":"S1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Three heads in six tosses","prompt":"A fair coin is tossed $6$ times. Find the probability of exactly $3$ heads.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3125},"hints":["n = 6, p = ½.","C(6, 3) = 20.","Divide by 64."],"ladder":{"nudge":"n = 6, p = ½.","method":"C(6, 3) = 20.","worked":"Divide by 64."},"steps":[{"h":"Binomial","d":"$\\binom63\\left(\\tfrac12\\right)^{6}=\\tfrac{20}{64}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5,"why":"Three heads is not half the probability.","expr":"1/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"5/16","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-017","group":"X12-S1-017","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"At most one success","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(10,0.2)$. Find $P(X\\le1)$, correct to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3758,"tol":0.00005},"hints":["At most one means 0 or 1.","Use the binomial formula.","Add."],"ladder":{"nudge":"At most one means 0 or 1.","method":"Use the binomial formula.","worked":"Add."},"steps":[{"h":"Add","d":"$0.8^{10}+10(0.2)(0.8)^{9}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.1074,"why":"Only P(X = 0)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"P(0) + P(1)","line":"0.8^10+10*0.2*0.8^9"},{"marks":1,"point":"0.3758","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-019","group":"X12-S1-019","dp":"S1.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Spread of a sample proportion","prompt":"Samples of size $84$ are taken from a population with $p=0.3$. Find the standard deviation of the sample proportion.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.05},"hints":["σ = √(p(1 − p)/n).","0.21/84 = 0.0025.","Square root."],"ladder":{"nudge":"σ = √(p(1 − p)/n).","method":"0.21/84 = 0.0025.","worked":"Square root."},"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.3\\times0.7}{84}}=\\sqrt{0.0025}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.0025,"why":"That is the variance."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.05","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-020","group":"X12-S1-020","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"How many tries to almost surely succeed","prompt":"Each trial fails with probability $0.3$. Find the least number of independent trials so that the probability that all fail is less than $0.001$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":6},"answerPrefix":"n =","hints":["All fail has probability 0.3ⁿ.","Use logs or test values.","Take the least n."],"ladder":{"nudge":"All fail has probability 0.3ⁿ.","method":"Use logs or test values.","worked":"$0.3^{n}<0.001$"},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$0.3^{n}<0.001$"},{"h":"Check","d":"$0.3^{5}=0.00243$, $0.3^{6}=0.000729$"}],"traps":[{"value":5,"why":"0.3⁵ is still above 0.001."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.3ⁿ < 0.001","line":"0.3^n < 0.001"},{"marks":1,"point":"6","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-022","group":"X12-S1-022","dp":"S1.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Proportion above sixty percent","prompt":"For samples of size $100$ from a population with $p=0.5$, use the normal approximation and the empirical rule to estimate $P(\\hat p>0.6)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.025},"hints":["Find σ of p̂.","How many SDs is 0.6 from 0.5?","One tail beyond 2 SD."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Find σ of p̂.","method":"How many SDs is 0.6 from 0.5?","worked":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.25}{100}}=0.05$"},"steps":[{"h":"SD","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.25}{100}}=0.05$"},{"h":"Tail","d":"$0.6$ is $2$ SD above: $\\tfrac{1-0.95}{2}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.05,"why":"That counts both tails."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"σ = 0.05","line":"sqrt(0.25/100)"},{"marks":1,"point":"0.025","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-023","group":"X12-S1-023","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Exactly two sixes","prompt":"A fair die is rolled $5$ times. Find the exact probability of exactly two sixes.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.16075102880658437},"hints":["n = 5, p = 1/6.","C(5, 2) = 10.","Simplify."],"ladder":{"nudge":"n = 5, p = 1/6.","method":"C(5, 2) = 10.","worked":"Simplify."},"steps":[{"h":"Binomial","d":"$\\binom52\\left(\\tfrac16\\right)^{2}\\left(\\tfrac56\\right)^{3}=\\tfrac{10\\cdot125}{7776}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.016075102880658436,"why":"Missed C(5, 2).","expr":"125/7776"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct expression","line":"C(5,2)*(1/6)^2*(5/6)^3"},{"marks":1,"point":"625/3888","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-025","group":"X12-S1-025","dp":"S1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Sample size for a target spread","prompt":"For a population with $p=0.2$, how large must the sample be for the standard deviation of $\\hat p$ to equal $0.02$?","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":400},"answerPrefix":"n =","hints":["σ = √(p(1 − p)/n).","Square both sides.","Solve for n."],"ladder":{"nudge":"σ = √(p(1 − p)/n).","method":"Square both sides.","worked":"Solve for n."},"steps":[{"h":"Equation","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.16}{n}}=0.02\\Rightarrow\\tfrac{0.16}{n}=0.0004$"}],"traps":[{"value":8,"why":"Did not square 0.02."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Squares both sides","line":"0.16/n = 0.0004"},{"marks":1,"point":"400","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-027","group":"X12-S1-027","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"At least two heads in five","prompt":"A fair coin is tossed $5$ times. Find the probability of at least $2$ heads.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.8125},"hints":["Use the complement.","P(0) = 1/32 and P(1) = 5/32.","Subtract."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Use the complement.","method":"P(0) = 1/32 and P(1) = 5/32.","worked":"Subtract."},"steps":[{"h":"Complement","d":"$1-\\tfrac1{32}-\\tfrac5{32}=\\tfrac{26}{32}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.96875,"why":"Only removed zero heads.","expr":"31/32"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Removes 0 and 1 heads","line":"1-1/32-5/32"},{"marks":1,"point":"13/16","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-029","group":"X12-S1-029","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Number of tosses from a zero probability","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(n,0.5)$ and $P(X=0)=\\tfrac{1}{64}$. Find $n$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":6},"answerPrefix":"n =","hints":["P(X = 0) = 0.5ⁿ.","64 = 2⁶.","Equate."],"ladder":{"nudge":"P(X = 0) = 0.5ⁿ.","method":"64 = 2⁶.","worked":"Equate."},"steps":[{"h":"Solve","d":"$0.5^{n}=\\tfrac1{64}=2^{-6}$"}],"traps":[{"value":64,"why":"Solved 1/n = 1/64."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"6","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-030","group":"X12-S1-030","dp":"S1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Two girls in four children","prompt":"Assuming each child is equally likely to be a boy or a girl, find the probability that a family of $4$ children has exactly $2$ girls.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.375},"hints":["n = 4, p = ½.","C(4, 2) = 6.","Divide by 16."],"ladder":{"nudge":"n = 4, p = ½.","method":"C(4, 2) = 6.","worked":"Divide by 16."},"steps":[{"h":"Binomial","d":"$\\binom42\\tfrac1{16}=\\tfrac6{16}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5,"why":"Two girls is not half the outcomes.","expr":"1/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"3/8","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-033","group":"X12-S1-033","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Two successes in eight trials","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(8,0.25)$. Find $P(X=2)$, correct to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3115,"tol":0.00005},"hints":["C(8, 2) = 28.","Powers of 0.25 and 0.75.","Multiply."],"ladder":{"nudge":"C(8, 2) = 28.","method":"Powers of 0.25 and 0.75.","worked":"Multiply."},"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$\\binom82(0.25)^{2}(0.75)^{6}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.0111,"why":"Missed C(8, 2)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.3115","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-035","group":"X12-S1-035","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Enough trials for a likely success","prompt":"Each trial succeeds with probability $0.1$. Find the least number of trials so that the probability of at least one success exceeds $0.9$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":22},"answerPrefix":"n =","hints":["Complement.","Take logs.","Round up."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Complement.","method":"Take logs.","worked":"$0.9^{n}<0.1$"},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$0.9^{n}<0.1$"},{"h":"Check","d":"$0.9^{21}\\approx0.109$, $0.9^{22}\\approx0.098$"}],"traps":[{"value":21,"why":"0.9²¹ is still above 0.1."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.9ⁿ < 0.1","line":"0.9^n < 0.1"},{"marks":1,"point":"22","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-036","group":"X12-S1-036","dp":"S1.2a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Spread of a sample proportion of two hundred","prompt":"Samples of size $200$ are taken from a population with $p=0.4$. Find the standard deviation of $\\hat p$, to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.0346,"tol":0.00005},"hints":["σ = √(p(1 − p)/n).","p(1 − p) = 0.24.","Square root."],"ladder":{"nudge":"σ = √(p(1 − p)/n).","method":"p(1 − p) = 0.24.","worked":"Square root."},"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.24}{200}}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.0012,"why":"That is the variance."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.0346","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-039","group":"X12-S1-039","dp":"S1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"All four succeed","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(4,0.9)$. Find $P(X=4)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.6561},"hints":["All four must succeed.","Multiply.","0.9⁴."],"ladder":{"nudge":"All four must succeed.","method":"Multiply.","worked":"0.9⁴."},"steps":[{"h":"All succeed","d":"$0.9^{4}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.9,"why":"That is one trial."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.6561","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-041","group":"X12-S1-041","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Most likely number of heads","prompt":"A fair coin is tossed $10$ times. Find the most likely number of heads and its probability.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.24609375},"hints":["The distribution is symmetric.","C(10, 5) = 252.","Divide by 2¹⁰."],"ladder":{"nudge":"The distribution is symmetric.","method":"C(10, 5) = 252.","worked":"Symmetric about $5$"},"steps":[{"h":"Mode","d":"Symmetric about $5$"},{"h":"Probability","d":"$\\tfrac{252}{1024}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5,"why":"Five heads is not half the probability.","expr":"1/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Mode 5","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"63/256","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-042","group":"X12-S1-042","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Number of tosses from at-least-one","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(n,0.5)$ and $P(X\\ge1)=\\tfrac{63}{64}$. Find $n$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":6},"answerPrefix":"n =","hints":["P(X = 0) = 1/64.","0.5ⁿ = 2⁻ⁿ.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"P(X = 0) = 1/64.","method":"0.5ⁿ = 2⁻ⁿ.","worked":"Solve."},"steps":[{"h":"Complement","d":"$0.5^{n}=\\tfrac{1}{64}$"}],"traps":[{"value":63,"why":"Read the numerator."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"6","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-046","group":"X12-S1-046","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"At most one defective","prompt":"Five percent of items are defective. In a sample of $10$, find $P(\\text{at most one defective})$, to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.9139,"tol":0.00006},"hints":["Bin(10, 0.05).","Add P(0) and P(1).","Evaluate."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Bin(10, 0.05).","method":"Add P(0) and P(1).","worked":"Evaluate."},"steps":[{"h":"Terms","d":"$0.95^{10}+10(0.05)(0.95)^{9}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5987,"why":"That is P(X = 0) only."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Both terms","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"0.9139","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-048","group":"X12-S1-048","dp":"S1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Normal approximation for a proportion above a value","prompt":"For a population with $p=0.4$, samples of size $96$ are taken. Using $P(Z>2)\\approx0.025$, find the approximate probability that $\\hat p>0.5$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.025},"hints":["SD of p̂.","Standardise.","Upper tail area."],"ladder":{"nudge":"SD of p̂.","method":"Standardise.","worked":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.24}{96}}=0.05$"},"steps":[{"h":"SD","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.24}{96}}=0.05$"},{"h":"z","d":"$\\tfrac{0.5-0.4}{0.05}=2$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.975,"why":"Upper tail."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"z = 2","line":"2"},{"marks":1,"point":"0.025","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-049","group":"X12-S1-049","dp":"S1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Binomial probability of exactly two","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(6,\\tfrac13)$. Find $P(X=2)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3292181069958848},"hints":["C(6, 2) = 15.","(1/3)² (2/3)⁴.","Multiply."],"ladder":{"nudge":"C(6, 2) = 15.","method":"(1/3)² (2/3)⁴.","worked":"Multiply."},"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$\\binom62\\left(\\tfrac13\\right)^{2}\\left(\\tfrac23\\right)^{4}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.02194787379972565,"why":"Include C(6, 2) = 15.","expr":"16/729"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"80/243","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-051","group":"X12-S1-051","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"At least two successes","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(5,0.2)$. Find $P(X\\ge2)$, to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.2627,"tol":0.00006},"hints":["1 − P(0) − P(1).","P(0) = 0.8⁵.","P(1) = 5(0.2)(0.8)⁴."],"ladder":{"nudge":"1 − P(0) − P(1).","method":"P(0) = 0.8⁵.","worked":"$1-0.8^{5}-5(0.2)(0.8)^{4}$"},"steps":[{"h":"Complement","d":"$1-0.8^{5}-5(0.2)(0.8)^{4}$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$1-0.32768-0.4096$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.6723,"why":"That is P(X ≥ 1)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Complement used","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"0.2627","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-054","group":"X12-S1-054","dp":"S1.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Most probable value of a binomial","prompt":"For $X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(10,0.3)$, find the most likely value of $X$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":3},"hints":["Compare P(k + 1) with P(k).","Solve the ratio > 1.","Mode near np."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Compare P(k + 1) with P(k).","method":"Solve the ratio > 1.","worked":"$\\dfrac{P(k+1)}{P(k)}=\\dfrac{(10-k)0.3}{(k+1)0.7}$"},"steps":[{"h":"Ratio","d":"$\\dfrac{P(k+1)}{P(k)}=\\dfrac{(10-k)0.3}{(k+1)0.7}$"},{"h":"Find","d":"Ratio $>1$ for $k\\le2$, $<1$ for $k\\ge3$"}],"traps":[{"value":0,"why":"Compare successive probabilities."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Ratio method or table","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"3","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-056","group":"X12-S1-056","dp":"S1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Binomial probability of all failures","prompt":"A test has a $0.85$ chance of detecting a fault. Five independent tests are run. Find the probability none detects it, to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.0000759,"tol":0.00005},"hints":["Each fails with 0.15.","Five independent.","Multiply."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Each fails with 0.15.","method":"Five independent.","worked":"Multiply."},"steps":[{"h":"All fail","d":"$0.15^{5}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.4437,"why":"That is 0.85⁵."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.0001","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-057","group":"X12-S1-057","dp":"S1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Sample proportion probability with a z table","prompt":"For $p=0.25$ and $n=75$, given $P(Z<1)=0.84$, find $P(\\hat p<0.3)$ approximately.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.84},"hints":["SD of p̂.","Standardise 0.3.","Read the table."],"ladder":{"nudge":"SD of p̂.","method":"Standardise 0.3.","worked":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.1875}{75}}=0.05$"},"steps":[{"h":"SD","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.1875}{75}}=0.05$"},{"h":"z","d":"$\\tfrac{0.05}{0.05}=1$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.16,"why":"Below, not above."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"z = 1","line":"1"},{"marks":1,"point":"0.84","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-058","group":"X12-S1-058","dp":"S1.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Binomial and conditional probability","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(3,0.5)$. Find $P(X=3\\mid X\\ge1)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.14285714285714285},"hints":["P(3) = 1/8.","P(≥1) = 7/8.","Divide."],"ladder":{"nudge":"P(3) = 1/8.","method":"P(≥1) = 7/8.","worked":"Divide."},"steps":[{"h":"Values","d":"$P(X=3)=\\tfrac18$, $P(X\\ge1)=\\tfrac78$"},{"h":"Divide","d":"$\\tfrac{1/8}{7/8}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.125,"why":"Condition on X ≥ 1.","expr":"1/8"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Both probabilities","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"1/7","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-059","group":"X12-S1-059","dp":"S1.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Binomial with complement for at least one","prompt":"The probability a seed germinates is $0.7$. Ten seeds are planted. Find the probability that at least one germinates, to six decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.9999941,"tol":0.000001},"hints":["Complement.","None germinate 0.3¹⁰.","Subtract."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Complement.","method":"None germinate 0.3¹⁰.","worked":"Subtract."},"steps":[{"h":"Complement","d":"$1-0.3^{10}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.7,"why":"That is one seed."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.999994","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-061","group":"X12-S1-061","dp":"S1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":1,"title":"Sample size for a given standard deviation","prompt":"For $p=0.5$, how large must $n$ be so that the standard deviation of $\\hat p$ is at most $0.02$?","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":625},"hints":["√(p(1 − p)/n) ≤ 0.02.","Square.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"√(p(1 − p)/n) ≤ 0.02.","method":"Square.","worked":"Solve."},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.25}{n}}\\le0.02\\Rightarrow n\\ge\\tfrac{0.25}{0.0004}$"}],"traps":[{"value":25,"why":"Square 0.02."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"625","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-065","group":"X12-S1-065","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Independent repeated trials until a success","prompt":"A player scores with probability $0.4$ on each attempt. Find the probability the first score is on the third attempt.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.144},"hints":["Two misses then a score.","Multiply.","Do not multiply by 3."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Two misses then a score.","method":"Multiply.","worked":"Sequence"},"steps":[{"h":"Sequence","d":"$0.6^{2}\\times0.4$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.288,"why":"Order is fixed: miss, miss, score."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.144","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-069","group":"X12-S1-069","dp":"S1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Probability a sample proportion exceeds a value","prompt":"For $p=0.6$ and $n=96$, using $P(Z<2)=0.977$, find the approximate probability that $\\hat p>0.7$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.023},"hints":["SD of p̂.","Standardise.","1 − 0.977."],"ladder":{"nudge":"SD of p̂.","method":"Standardise.","worked":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.24}{96}}=0.05$"},"steps":[{"h":"SD","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.24}{96}}=0.05$"},{"h":"z","d":"$\\tfrac{0.1}{0.05}=2$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.977,"why":"Upper tail."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"z = 2","line":"2"},{"marks":1,"point":"0.023","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-070","group":"X12-S1-070","dp":"S1.2a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Required sample size for a margin","prompt":"For $p=0.3$, find the least $n$ so that $2\\sqrt{\\tfrac{p(1-p)}{n}}\\le0.05$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":336},"hints":["Divide by 2.","Square.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Divide by 2.","method":"Square.","worked":"$\\tfrac{0.21}{n}\\le0.000625$"},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$\\tfrac{0.21}{n}\\le0.000625$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$n\\ge336$"}],"traps":[{"value":84,"why":"Square 0.025."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Inequality","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"336","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-072","group":"X12-S1-072","dp":"S1.2a","authored":5,"level":4,"marks":1,"title":"Comparing two sample sizes","prompt":"By what factor must the sample size increase to halve the standard deviation of $\\hat p$? Justify.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":4},"hints":["SD = √(p(1 − p)/n).","Halve means √n doubles.","n quadruples."],"ladder":{"nudge":"SD = √(p(1 − p)/n).","method":"Halve means √n doubles.","worked":"n quadruples."},"steps":[{"h":"Scaling","d":"SD $\\propto\\tfrac{1}{\\sqrt n}$"}],"traps":[{"value":2,"why":"SD scales with 1/√n."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"4","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-073","group":"X12-S1-073","dp":"S1.1a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Smallest number of trials for at least one success","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(n,0.3)$. Find the least $n$ so that $P(X\\ge1)>0.95$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":9},"hints":["Complement is no successes.","Take logs.","Inequality flips (ln 0.7 < 0)."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Complement is no successes.","method":"Take logs.","worked":"$0.7^{n}<0.05$"},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$0.7^{n}<0.05$"},{"h":"Logs","d":"$n>\\dfrac{\\ln0.05}{\\ln0.7}\\approx8.4$"}],"traps":[{"value":8,"why":"n must exceed 8.4."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Inequality","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"9","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-074","group":"X12-S1-074","dp":"S1.1a","authored":5,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Binomial parameter from equal probabilities","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(10,p)$ with $0<p<1$ and $P(X=1)=P(X=2)$. Find $p$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.18181818181818182},"hints":["Write both probabilities.","Cancel p(1 − p)⁸.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Write both probabilities.","method":"Cancel p(1 − p)⁸.","worked":"$10p(1-p)^{9}=45p^{2}(1-p)^{8}$"},"steps":[{"h":"Equation","d":"$10p(1-p)^{9}=45p^{2}(1-p)^{8}$"},{"h":"Simplify","d":"$10(1-p)=45p$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.2222222222222222,"why":"Collect 55p = 10.","expr":"2/9"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Equation","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"2/11","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-075","group":"X12-S1-075","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Binomial probability of exactly two","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(5,0.4)$. Find $P(X=2)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3456},"hints":["C(5,2) = 10.","0.4² × 0.6³.","Multiply."],"ladder":{"nudge":"C(5,2) = 10.","method":"0.4² × 0.6³.","worked":"Multiply."},"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$\\binom52(0.4)^{2}(0.6)^{3}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.2304,"why":"Use 0.6³ for three failures."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.3456","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-081","group":"X12-S1-081","dp":"S1.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"At most one success","prompt":"$X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(6,0.1)$. Find $P(X\\le1)$ to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.885735,"tol":0.00006},"hints":["P(0) + P(1).","Binomial formula.","Add."],"ladder":{"nudge":"P(0) + P(1).","method":"Binomial formula.","worked":"Add."},"steps":[{"h":"Terms","d":"$0.9^{6}+6(0.1)(0.9)^{5}$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$0.5314+0.3543$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.5314,"why":"Include X = 1."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Two terms","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"0.8857","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-082","group":"X12-S1-082","dp":"S1.2a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Sample size for a precise proportion","prompt":"For $p=0.5$, find the smallest sample size $n$ for which the standard deviation of $\\hat p$ is at most $0.02$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":625},"hints":["SD formula.","Square both sides.","Solve."],"ladder":{"nudge":"SD formula.","method":"Square both sides.","worked":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.25}{n}}\\le0.02$"},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.25}{n}}\\le0.02$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$n\\ge\\tfrac{0.25}{0.0004}$"}],"traps":[{"value":25,"why":"Square 0.02."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Inequality","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"625","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-083","group":"X12-S1-083","dp":"S1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Lower-tail sample proportion probability","prompt":"Samples of $96$ are taken with $p=0.6$. Using a normal approximation and $P(Z<1)=0.8413$, find $P(\\hat p<0.55)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.1587},"hints":["SD 0.05.","z = −1.","Symmetry."],"ladder":{"nudge":"SD 0.05.","method":"z = −1.","worked":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.24}{96}}=0.05$"},"steps":[{"h":"SD","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.24}{96}}=0.05$"},{"h":"z","d":"$-1$; $1-0.8413$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.8413,"why":"Lower tail."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"SD and z","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"0.1587","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-085","group":"X12-S1-085","dp":"S1.1a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"At least two sixes","prompt":"A fair die is rolled $10$ times. Find the probability of at least two sixes, to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.51548,"tol":0.00006},"hints":["Complement of 0 or 1.","Binomial terms.","Subtract."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Complement of 0 or 1.","method":"Binomial terms.","worked":"$1-P(0)-P(1)$"},"steps":[{"h":"Complement","d":"$1-P(0)-P(1)$"},{"h":"Terms","d":"$\\left(\\tfrac56\\right)^{10}+10\\left(\\tfrac16\\right)\\left(\\tfrac56\\right)^{9}$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$1-0.1615-0.3230$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.8385,"why":"Also subtract P(X = 1)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Complement","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Both terms","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"0.5155","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-087","group":"X12-S1-087","dp":"S1.2a","authored":5,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Sample size for a tail probability","prompt":"With $p=0.4$, find the smallest sample size $n$ for which $P(\\hat p\\ge0.5)\\le0.025$, using a normal approximation and $P(Z\\ge1.96)=0.025$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":93},"hints":["Standardise 0.5.","z ≥ 1.96.","Solve for n."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Standardise 0.5.","method":"z ≥ 1.96.","worked":"$\\dfrac{0.1}{\\sqrt{0.24/n}}\\ge1.96$"},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$\\dfrac{0.1}{\\sqrt{0.24/n}}\\ge1.96$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$n\\ge\\left(\\dfrac{1.96\\sqrt{0.24}}{0.1}\\right)^{2}\\approx92.2$"},{"h":"Round up","d":"$93$"}],"traps":[{"value":92,"why":"Round up to satisfy the inequality."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Inequality","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"92.2","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"93","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-092","group":"X12-S1-092","dp":"S1.1a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Number of trials from a probability of no success","prompt":"For $X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(n,0.1)$, find the least $n$ with $P(X=0)<0.5$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":7},"hints":["P(X = 0) = 0.9ⁿ.","Take logs.","Round up."],"ladder":{"nudge":"P(X = 0) = 0.9ⁿ.","method":"Take logs.","worked":"$0.9^{n}<0.5$"},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$0.9^{n}<0.5$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$n>6.58$"}],"traps":[{"value":6,"why":"0.9⁶ ≈ 0.53 > 0.5."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Inequality","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"7","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-100","group":"X12-S1-100","dp":"S1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":1,"title":"Increasing the sample size","prompt":"By what factor must the sample size be increased to halve the standard deviation of $\\hat p$?","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":4},"hints":["SD = √(p(1 − p)/n).","Halve means √n doubles.","n × 4."],"ladder":{"nudge":"SD = √(p(1 − p)/n).","method":"Halve means √n doubles.","worked":"n × 4."},"steps":[{"h":"Reason","d":"SD $\\propto\\tfrac1{\\sqrt n}$"}],"traps":[{"value":2,"why":"SD depends on √n."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"4","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-103","group":"X12-S1-103","dp":"S1.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Exactly two successes in ten","prompt":"If $X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(10,0.3)$, find $P(X=2)$ to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.2335,"tol":0.0001},"hints":["C(10, 2) = 45.","0.09.","0.7⁸."],"ladder":{"nudge":"C(10, 2) = 45.","method":"0.09.","worked":"0.7⁸."},"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$\\binom{10}2(0.3)^{2}(0.7)^{8}$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"0.2335","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-105","group":"X12-S1-105","dp":"S1.2a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Sample proportion above forty six percent","prompt":"In a population $40\\%$ have a trait. For random samples of $150$, use a normal approximation to find $P(\\hat p>0.46)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.0668,"tol":0.001},"hints":["σ = √(p(1−p)/n).","z = 1.5.","Upper tail."],"ladder":{"nudge":"σ = √(p(1−p)/n).","method":"z = 1.5.","worked":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.4\\times0.6}{150}}=0.04$"},"steps":[{"h":"Spread","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.4\\times0.6}{150}}=0.04$"},{"h":"Standardise","d":"$z=\\tfrac{0.06}{0.04}=1.5$"},{"h":"Probability","d":"$1-0.9332$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Standard deviation","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"z-score","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"0.0668","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-106","group":"X12-S1-106","dp":"S1.1a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Trials for ninety nine percent chance of a success","prompt":"Each trial succeeds with probability $0.15$. Find the least number of independent trials so that the probability of at least one success exceeds $0.99$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":29},"hints":["Complement.","Logs.","Inequality flips."],"ladder":{"nudge":"Complement.","method":"Logs.","worked":"$0.85^{n}<0.01$"},"steps":[{"h":"Inequality","d":"$0.85^{n}<0.01$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$n>\\dfrac{\\ln0.01}{\\ln0.85}\\approx28.3$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Inequality","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"29","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-107","group":"X12-S1-107","dp":"S1.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"At most one success in eight","prompt":"If $X\\sim\\mathrm{Bin}(8,0.25)$, find $P(X\\le1)$ to four decimal places.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.3671,"tol":0.0001},"hints":["X = 0 and X = 1.","Binomial formula.","Add."],"ladder":{"nudge":"X = 0 and X = 1.","method":"Binomial formula.","worked":"Add."},"steps":[{"h":"Terms","d":"$0.75^{8}+8(0.25)(0.75)^{7}$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Both terms","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"0.3671","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-108","group":"X12-S1-108","dp":"S1.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Coin sample proportion below forty seven percent","prompt":"A fair coin is tossed $400$ times. Use a normal approximation to estimate the probability that the proportion of heads is less than $0.47$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.1151,"tol":0.002},"hints":["σ = 0.025.","(0.47 − 0.5)/0.025.","Lower tail."],"ladder":{"nudge":"σ = 0.025.","method":"Standardise","worked":"Lower tail."},"steps":[{"h":"Spread","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.25}{400}}=0.025$"},{"h":"Standardise","d":"$z=-1.2$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"z-score","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"0.1151","answer":true}]},{"id":"X12-S1-110","group":"X12-S1-110","dp":"S1.2a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Poll support of at least sixty five percent","prompt":"$60\\%$ of voters support a policy. For random samples of $250$, use a normal approximation to estimate $P(\\hat p\\ge0.65)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.053,"tol":0.002},"hints":["σ = √(pq/n).","Standardise.","Upper tail."],"ladder":{"nudge":"σ = √(pq/n).","method":"Standardise.","worked":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.24}{250}}\\approx0.0310$"},"steps":[{"h":"Spread","d":"$\\sqrt{\\tfrac{0.24}{250}}\\approx0.0310$"},{"h":"z","d":"$\\tfrac{0.05}{0.0310}\\approx1.61$"},{"h":"Probability","d":"$1-0.947$"}],"traps":[],"crite